    <!-- Privacy -->
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy &amp; licenses</string>
    <string name="privacy_data_title">Data handling</string>
    <string name="privacy_data_body">SOS Ring processes call and contact data on your device. If you enable VIP message alerts, notification metadata is processed locally to identify paired direct conversations; message text, contact names and phone numbers from notifications are never stored. Only hashed conversation identifiers and technical deduplication fingerprints are saved.\n\nLocation sharing uses a peer-to-peer channel (ntfy). Coordinates are encrypted end-to-end with AES-256-GCM using a per-device key generated locally and shared with trusted family via QR.\n\nThe server (ntfy) never knows your key. If you lose your phone without a key backup, encrypted messages cannot be recovered.\n\nThis is NOT forward-secret and does NOT protect against a compromised phone, malware, screenshots, or keyloggers.\n\nNo analytics, no tracking, no ads.</string>
